EXPERIMENT 13 – AUTOMATING WEB FORM FILLING AND SUBMISSION USING SELENIUM

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to automate the filling and submission of a web form.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Open the sample web form page.
3. Enter text, password and comment using sendKeys().
4. Click the Submit button using click().
5. Read the heading and message of the result page.
6. Close the browser.
CODE
Exercise13.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;

public class Exercise13 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            driver.get(
                "https://www.selenium.dev/selenium/web/web-form.html"
            );

            System.out.println("Page title : " + driver.getTitle());

            driver.findElement(By.name("my-text"))
                .sendKeys("Student");

            driver.findElement(By.name("my-password"))
                .sendKeys("Secret@123");

            driver.findElement(By.name("my-textarea"))
                .sendKeys("Automated using Selenium WebDriver");

            driver.findElement(
                By.cssSelector("button[type='submit']")
            ).click();

            System.out.println("Heading : " +
                driver.findElement(By.tagName("h1")).getText());

            System.out.println("Message : " +
                driver.findElement(By.id("message")).getText());

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
Field	Input
Text	Student
Password	Secret@123
Comment	Automated using Selenium WebDriver

OUTPUT
Page title : Web form
Heading : Form submitted
Message : Received!


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to automate the filling and submission of a web form was executed successfully and the output was verified.
